--TEST--
`prepareRename` on a built-in type in a local declaration's annotation is refused, because a built-in type is declared nowhere in the workspace, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
array<mi<|>xed> $rows = [1, 2, 3];
--REQUEST--
prepareRename
--EXPECT--
refused: There is nothing to rename here. You can rename a class, a variable, a method, a property, a constant or an enum case.
